window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><i>Some prophecies are sacred.<br> <br> Some are silenced.<br> She was never supposed to survive either.</i><br> <br> They said the last child born under a blood moon would bring ruin. So, they killed her before she could take her first breath.<br> <br> Or so they thought.<br> Sixteen years later, she walks in a city built on secrets—where vampires rule in shadow, and the old magic is sealed behind bones and burned pages. She has no fangs. No clan. Just hunger that doesn’t belong to her and voices in her blood that speak of fire and ruin.<br> <br> When a ritual goes wrong and her name is spoken by a dying Seer, the Prophets come hunting—not to protect her, but to erase her.<br> <br> But this time, she won’t die quietly.<br> <br> Because the prophecy wasn’t wrong.<br> <br> It was broken.<br> And she’s here to finish what they started.</p>"; 
